+### NEW 2026-08-31 (outer-loop, MEASURED) — THE ADAPTER-FREE EVAL RECORDS NO PER-GAME GENERATOR PROVENANCE, SO A 9-GAME RUN IS UNINTERPRETABLE
+
+A 22-hour adapter-free run of `scripts/arc_leaderboard_eval.py --policy e3` over the CLAIMED set
+produced per-game numbers that CANNOT be read as an e3 result, because nothing records whether
+each game actually had a generator.
+
+**What the run reported** (`results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs/*.json`):
+
+| game | levels | efficiency | generator verified? |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| cd82 | 2 | 0.0267 | YES — fit with FFN_CPU_LAYERS=1 |
+| r11l | 2 | 0.6890 | YES — same launch |
+| lp85 | 1 | 0.0039 | unknown |
+| ls20 | 0 | 0.0 | partly — a live socket to the shared server was observed once |
+| wa30 | 0 | 0.0 | unknown |
+| sp80 | 1 | 0.0661 | unknown (TWO conflicting files exist) |
+| su15 | 1 | 0.0042/0.0050 | unknown (differs between the two files) |
+| tu93 | 2 | 0.1025 | unknown — and NO per-run file was written |
+| cn04 | — | — | no line at all |
+| m0r0 | 0 | 0.0008 | unknown |
+| sk48 | 0 | 0.0 | unknown |
+
+**The mechanism.** One `llama-server` fit at first launch (23,579 MiB free, auto-selecting one
+CPU-FFN layer). It then held ~18.4 GB for the whole run, so every later game logged
+
+    CUDA gpu1 has 5155 MiB free; even 12 CPU-FFN layers cannot fit the generator
+
+and failed to load its own. **Of 23 server logs from this run, exactly ONE has any
+`print_timing` lines (32,833); the other 22 have zero** — they are failed starts that spawned a
+log and died. Whether a later game then reached the surviving server over HTTP is the crux, and
+it was directly confirmed exactly once (an ESTABLISHED socket from batch 2 to port 8919 on
+08-31 ~09:57Z).
+
+**Why the artifacts cannot settle it.** The per-game rows carry NO llm, induction, generator or
+proposer field of any kind. A row showing `levels=2, eff=0.1025` is indistinguishable between
+"the e3 cascade solved it" and "the explorer floor solved it with no model at all".
+
+**Two corrections to my own earlier reasoning, recorded because both were confidently stated.**
+On 08-31 ~09:57Z I concluded the reused server was harmless because a live socket proved a batch
+was using it — true, and it missed that the same reuse denied every LATER batch its own
+generator. Earlier still I read `ppid 1` as abandonment and nearly killed it mid-run. The reused
+server was both load-bearing AND harmful, at different times, and each single observation
+supported only half of that.
+
+**Task: record per-game generator provenance in the eval artifact.** Minimum: the resolved
+backend (in-process vs shared-server URL), whether a model load succeeded, and a count of
+completions actually consumed. Without it no multi-game run of this script is interpretable, and
+the 22 hours above bought two trustworthy games.
+
+**Do NOT cite `7 levels across 9 games` as an adapter-free e3 result.** The dashboard's
+`generaliz.` line currently reports it and is unreliable for the same reason; only cd82 (2 levels,
+0.0267) and r11l (2 levels, 0.6890) are defensible, and r11l is the outlier that made the set look
+encouraging.
+
